# Scoped to ui/ deliberately (story c2-1, AC 10).
#
# The repository has core.autocrlf=true and no root .gitattributes, so without this file
# ui/ checks out CRLF on Windows and LF on ubuntu CI. Prettier's `endOfLine: "lf"` treats
# CRLF as a formatting violation, which makes `prettier --check` red for the project lead
# and green in CI from the same commit — worse than no gate at all.
#
# A root-level .gitattributes would renormalise every tracked file in the repository, which
# is not this story's change. Setting prettier's `endOfLine: "auto"` was the alternative and
# was rejected: it lets CRLF and LF both pass, and c2-2/c2-3's `git diff --exit-code` drift
# checks need one deterministic byte sequence.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must not be normalised.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
